    "summary_insights": [
      "The asset base significantly expanded with tangible assets increasing from £45,607 to £332,464, primarily driven by substantial investment in plant and machinery.",
      "Liquidity has tightened, with the current ratio falling from 1.76 to 1.52 and the quick ratio dropping from 1.34 to 1.00, indicating less headroom for short-term obligations.",
      "Net current assets decreased from £168,371 to £152,719, as current liabilities grew faster than current assets.",
      "The capital structure has shifted heavily toward debt; the gearing ratio surged from 30% to 193% due to a large increase in long-term hire purchase liabilities.",
      "Net assets remained stable with a marginal growth of 0.78%, as the year's profit of £53,890 was largely offset by dividends of £52,608.",
      "A significant red flag is the sharp rise in long-term liabilities and deferred taxation, which may impact future cash flows and borrowing capacity."
